{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_fa54732ef18b76d8\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_fa54732ef18b76d8/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Instruction-following vs accuracy tradeoff\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_6b0a2b0015aa474bf50996d0\", \"member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks which response wins when one follows the format and the other is more accurate.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether accuracy can outweigh ignoring the user's requested output structure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the tutor's thread, a QA tutor asks whether instruction-following severity can be separated from factual-accuracy severity.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the tutor's thread says the format requirement was explicit in the prompt rather than optional.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the tutor's thread, the team lead requests the exact formatting instruction so QA can verify whether it was mandatory before weighing the responses, rather than comparing only output style.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and FAQ require separate scoring of accuracy and instruction following and identification of whether the requested structure was mandatory. A required structure is not optional, but no universal preference ordering is established. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects for a team lead decision; do not assume facts about the other response.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied threads do not include the exact formatting instruction or both responses, and neither records a preference decision; the team lead's requested input in the tutor's thread remains missing.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval records a team lead decision covering the batch-14 calibration exercise, not a new preference threshold; that approval does not record completion or an outcome.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The batch-14 announcement asks reviewers to keep material factual and instruction-following defects separate and bring both rationales for disputed pairs to its eight-pair calibration review; it does not establish a batch-15 review destination.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor and a tutor ask how to choose between stronger accuracy and compliance with a requested format.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance requires separate scoring of those dimensions, not a universal priority rule; a preference decision needs the actual prompt and both responses when the applicable rules do not settle it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the tutor's thread, a QA tutor also asks whether instruction-following severity can be separated from factual-accuracy severity.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor in that thread says the format requirement was explicit, but the team lead asks for the exact formatting instruction so QA can verify whether it was mandatory before weighing the responses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"detail:d1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The supplied threads contain neither the requested exact instruction nor both responses, and neither thread records a preference decision.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a clarification answering both threads with the separate-scoring rule and the case evidence needed before choosing a preference. Draft to copy: For the accuracy-versus-format questions raised by a QA tutor and a tutor: score factual accuracy and instruction following separately, and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. A required structure is not optional, but there is no universal rule that accuracy or format always wins. For each comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects. If the applicable rules and actual pair still do not settle the preference, I can confirm the decision. In the tutor's thread, please also paste the exact formatting instruction I requested so QA can verify whether it was mandatory. Scope: Clarify the existing project-wide rule without choosing either response or extending the tutor-thread instruction to the other thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Current guidance answers how to score the dimensions but deliberately provides no universal winner. A clarification addresses the repeated scoring question without deciding incomplete comparisons.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): A QA tutor and a tutor raise the same consequential preference question across two threads, without a recorded answer choosing between the responses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_6b0a2b0015aa474bf50996d0\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_6b0a2b0015aa474bf50996d0 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor's supplied thread contains the preference question and no answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead gives the tutor a concrete next step to verify whether the structure was mandatory, but the requested instruction and a preference decision are absent from the supplied thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: A QA tutor and a tutor repeatedly ask how to weigh defects that can change the selected response. This is meaningful scoring uncertainty, but the messages do not show incorrect labels, blocked work or batch-wide disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[0]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\\\": A QA tutor asks which response wins when format compliance and accuracy differ; a tutor asks the same preference question in a separate thread the next day. The uncertainty concerns the selected response, not merely wording.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790856332.000018\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_6b0a2b0015aa474bf50996d0\", \"thread_id\": \"1790856332.000018\", \"author_id\": \"U019\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T12:05:32.000018Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U019\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Could QA clarify this case: A follows format, B is more accurate. Which wins?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932885.000015\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\", \"thread_id\": \"1790932885.000015\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T09:21:25.000015Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can accuracy outweigh ignoring the user's requested output structure?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932935.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\", \"thread_id\": \"1790932885.000015\", \"author_id\": \"U013\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T09:22:15.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thumbsup\", \"users\": [\"U017\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"The format requirement was explicit in the user prompt, not an optional preference.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790932979.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\", \"thread_id\": \"1790932885.000015\", \"author_id\": \"U019\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T09:22:59.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can we separate instruction-following severity from factual-accuracy severity?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790933024.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b0a066a9dcba609a9aebaec9\", \"thread_id\": \"1790932885.000015\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T09:23:44.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Please paste the exact formatting instruction; QA needs to verify whether it was mandatory before weighing the responses. We need to compare the actual user instruction, not only the output style.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction following\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction following\\n\\n### Q: The prompt required JSON, but one response is well-written prose. Which response wins?\\nThe required format is not optional: record its violation separately from factual accuracy. No universal tie-break rule is established for competing accuracy and instruction-following defects. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the preference, provide the prompt and both responses for TL confirmation.\\n\\n### Q: Can accuracy outweigh ignoring a requested output structure?\\nScore the dimensions separately and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. Do not infer a general priority rule from one example or decide without the other response's evidence.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction adherence versus accuracy\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction adherence versus accuracy\\nScore these dimensions separately. An explicit required output structure, such as JSON, is not optional.\\n\\nThis guidance does not define a universal preference ordering for a response that is stronger on accuracy but weaker on a required format. When the applicable rules and actual pair do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects for a TL decision. Do not assume facts about the other response.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-16T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_14): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nPreference batch 14 calibration: choose a tie when neither answer offers a meaningful quality advantage. If choosing A or B, identify the user-facing benefit rather than saying only that it sounds nicer. Keep material factual or instruction-following defects separate. Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review. This message clarifies the existing criterion; it does not create a new numerical threshold.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:4745e3e0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Project purpose\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false